WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:02.780
POLICE RAID:
January 20, 2012.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:09.890
The New Zealand police uses their anti-terrorism
special tactics group to illegally raid a

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:15.040
$32 million mansion with 76 officers and 2
helicopters.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.040
Reason?

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.720
A special request from the FBI.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.080
Target?

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.890
Kim Dotcom, an apparant international terrorist.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:31.050
The police would not only arrest Kim but also
seize 18 luxury cars, $175 million in cash,

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.739
and 64 of his bank accounts.

00:00:33.739 --> 00:00:36.899
This wasn’t just some random off the cuff
raid either.

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:42.280
New Zealand’s Security Bureau had been stalking
Kim for weeks before the raid, but those few

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.920
weeks were nothing.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.949
Rumors started flying around that the prime
minister of New Zealand, John Key, was in

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:50.129
on the plan for years.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:55.199
Apparently, the only reason he granted Kim
residency in the first place was so that he

00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:58.100
could one day raid and extradite Kim.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.500
It wasn’t just New Zealand’s PM that was
allegedly in on the plan either.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.470
US president Barack Obama had allegedly been
colluding with Hollywood the entire time to

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.090
orchestrate the entire plan.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.390
What did Kim do that was so vile and apprehensible?

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:19.690
Well, he was the infamous founder of piracy
site MegaUpload and later Mega.nz.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:26.729
During its hayday, MegaUpload had more than
150 million registered users, 50 million daily

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:32.060
visitors, and it accounted for 4% of the entire
internet’s total traffic.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:38.909
As such, MegaUpload had lost copyright holders
more than $500 million making Kim an international

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:44.479
fugitive wanted for copyright infringement,
money laundering, racketeering, and wire fraud.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:49.310
Unlike the Pirate Bay’s founders though,
Kim wasn’t running MegaUpload out of principle.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:54.490
He was running MegaUpload as a business and
a very lucrative one at that.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:02:00.659
He had a net worth of atleast $200 million
and he wasn’t gonna go down without a fight.

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:04.549
Over the next several years, he would wage
one of the most expensive court battles in

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:08.580
New Zealand history and come out rather victorious.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.459
He would get New Zealand to admit that they
were illegally spying on him, that the raid

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:17.330
used excessive force, and that the seizure
of his property was unjust.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:22.890
And to this day, 11 years later, Kim Dotcom
is still a free man in New Zealand that has

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.170
yet to be extradited.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:30.489
So, here’s the insane story of MegaUpload
founder, Kim Dotcom: the internet legend that’s

00:02:30.489 --> 00:02:33.980
classified as a terrorist.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:42.950
THE NERD HACKER:
Taking a look back, the story of Kim dates

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.129
back to January 21, 1974.

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:51.310
His real name is Kim Schmitz and he was born
to an ordinary family in Kiel, West Germany.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:53.890
But, nothing about Kim was ordinary.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:59.240
In fact, he was a trouble maker from very
early on as he had an interest in hacking.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:05.370
And when I say hacking, I don’t mean Webkinz
hacking, I mean Mr. Robot type hacking.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:10.459
In his teens, Kim claims to have hacked hundreds
of US companies including the likes of NASA,

00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:13.210
the Pentagon, and Citibank.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:17.920
Apparently, he would hack into their PBX systems
which were wide open doors for him.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:23.130
He would then turn around and sell the access
codes to these systems for $200 a piece.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:29.010
Kim would boast about his hacking skills on
German TV but to be honest, I don’t think

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:34.310
selling access codes to the Pentagon for only
$200 is something to brag about.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:39.090
I mean, the real person getting robbed there
is Kim but I digress.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.700
Aside from selling these access codes, Kim
would also sell encrypted phones that couldn’t

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.080
be tapped likely to some pretty shady figures.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.620
But, somehow neither of these landed Kim in
any trouble.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.100
Something that did land him in trouble though
was yet another scheme with calling cards.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.250
Kim would buy stolen calling cards from American
hackers for cheap and then sell them for full

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.950
price in Hong Kong and the Carribean.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:08.599
This made him a cool €61,000 in his teens
but it also landed him in jail in March of

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:10.239
1994.

00:04:10.239 --> 00:04:15.110
This would result in 11 counts of computer
fraud, 10 counts of data espionage, and several

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.910
other charges as well.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:21.639
Normally, this would land someone in jail
for several months if not over a year, but

00:04:21.639 --> 00:04:25.020
given Kim’s age, the judge would go easy
on him.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:30.450
He would give Kim a 2 year suspended sentence
which means that Kim didn’t have to go to

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.450
jail.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.669
But, if he broke the law again within the
next 2 years, he would have to serve time

00:04:34.669 --> 00:04:37.690
for the original crimes and the new crime.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:42.950
Kim had escaped jail time with the skin of
his teeth but his life was basically ruined.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:47.890
I mean, he literally had a criminal record
by the time he was 20 making him virtually

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:51.860
unhirable, or atleast that would be the case
for most people.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:55.980
Kim, however, wore his criminal record as
a badge of honor.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.710
From his perspective, being wanted by the
police at such a young age was simply a testament

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.770
to how good his hacking skills were.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:07.520
In fact, he would use this reputation to open
an cybersecurity consulting business called

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:11.650
Data Protect and one of his first clients
was Lufthansa airlines.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.880
Kim likes to claim that he dazzled Lufthansa
with his hacking skills.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:21.680
Other sources claim that he knew an insider
but either way Kim was soon pulling in millions

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.090
and his lifestyle would reflect this.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:29.540
He would of course buy supercars, mansions,
yachts, and all the regular stuff but he also

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:33.150
spent a bunch of money on creating an online
persona.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:37.210
You could say that Kim was the first Instagram
flexer in the world.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:42.770
Kim was definitely not the most humble guy
out there which made one thing clear: he was

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:48.220
no longer the nerd hacker, he was now the
rich hacker.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:59.770
THE RICH HACKER:
Now that Kim had a somewhat legitimate IT

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:04.889
business, you would think that he would play
it safe and stay out of trouble but that just

00:06:04.889 --> 00:06:06.490
wasn’t Kim’s style.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:12.419
Pretty soon, he would be caught up in a pump
a dump scheme with a company called letsbuyit.com.

00:06:12.419 --> 00:06:16.470
Letsbuyit was basically a wanna be Amazon
back in the dotcom days.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:21.670
After dotcom funding dried up though, the
company would soon by on the verge of bankruptcy.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:27.039
Instead of letting the company go bankrupt
though, Kim would go ahead and invest €375,000

00:06:27.039 --> 00:06:29.360
into the company in 2001.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:34.300
On top of this, he would claim that he was
gonna bring on investors with €50 million

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.810
and that they were gonna stage a turnaround.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:42.569
This would of course cause the stock to go
wild but the turnaround nor the 50 million

00:06:42.569 --> 00:06:43.650
ever came.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:48.509
The only thing that happened was Kim would
walk away with a €1.5 million profit from

00:06:48.509 --> 00:06:49.509
the pump.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:52.580
This wasn’t the only scheme that Kim pulled
off either.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:56.900
He would also launch a fintech companies called
Monkey AG and Monkeybank.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:01.930
To be honest, I’m not really sure what these
companies even did but what we do know is

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:06.440
that Kim would embezzle a few hundred thousand
euros from them which made him a prime target

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.470
for the police.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:12.150
Fearful about his freedom, Kim would flee
to Thailand and stage a massive publicity

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.150
stunt.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:17.310
He would claim that he had hacked into Mr.
Small Beard’s Sudanese bank account.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:22.450
He would also put up prize money of $10 million
for any information regarding Mr. Small Beard.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:28.090
But, this publicity stunt didn’t exactly
win him much support and so he would just

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.250
turn to faking his death online.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:35.080
Unfortunatley, this too didn’t work and
Kim would be deported back to Germany and

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.800
put in jail in November of 2003.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:41.979
This time, he would spend 5 months in jail
awaiting his trial before getting off with

00:07:41.979 --> 00:07:46.720
another slap on the wrist: yet another suspended
sentence of 20 months.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:50.360
Kim became convinced that what was holding
him back was Germany.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.979
What he needed was a change in scenery.

00:07:52.979 --> 00:07:58.210
And with that, he would move to Hong Kong
in 2003 to continue his shady activities.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:03.060
He would open up a new business called Trendax
that was apparently supposed to use AI to

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:06.909
generate unbelievable returns of 25% per year.

00:08:06.909 --> 00:08:08.940
But, that was complete BS.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:14.870
In fact, the $250,000 that Kim did spend on
the business mostly went towards design and

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:19.620
theatrics as opposed to creating an AI system
that actually worked.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.639
Little to say, no one signed up.

00:08:21.639 --> 00:08:27.270
In fact, the company never even got permission
to accept investor funds, so it was a complete

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.270
failure.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:33.610
But, while his real life fortune was crumbling,
Kim would continue keeping up his persona

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.610
online.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.990
For example, he would produce a couple of
bizarre animations that poked fun at Bill

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.050
Gates.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:43.110
In a flash animation called Kimble Special
Agent for example, he would break into Bill

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:46.240
Gates’ house and write the word Linux on
his walls.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.890
In another film called Kimble goes Monaco,
Kim would go on vacation only to constantly

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.240
catch Bill Gates spying on him.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:59.019
This was mostly just satire at the time but
this has ended up being surprisingly accurate.

00:08:59.019 --> 00:09:04.100
But, while these films got Kim some internet
points, the truth was that his real life was

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.370
quickly falling apart.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:10.769
In fact, he had stooped as low as going to
airports just so that he could take pictures

00:09:10.769 --> 00:09:12.279
in parked airplanes.

00:09:12.279 --> 00:09:17.519
Clearly, he was desperate and this desperateness
would transform him from being a rich hacker

00:09:17.519 --> 00:09:21.089
to being a criminal hacker.

00:09:21.089 --> 00:09:33.100
THE CRIMINAL HACKER:
In 2005, Kim would officially change his name

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:38.459
from Kim Schmitz to Kim Dotcom and this marked
the beginning of piracy days.

00:09:38.459 --> 00:09:43.829
He would change the name of his IT company,
Data Protect, to MegaUpload and launch a website

00:09:43.829 --> 00:09:45.370
centered around file sharing.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:50.230
Honestly, he was pretty early to the whole
file sharing thing, so he could’ve easily

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:55.730
created a legitimate file sharing platform
like Dropbox which was created 2 years after

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:56.730
MegaUpload.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:10:02.200
I mean technically, if you ask Kim or especially
any of his lawyers, they’ll assure you that

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:07.089
MegaUpload is indeed a legitimate file sharing
platform that has no intention of breaking

00:10:07.089 --> 00:10:10.910
copyright regulation but you can take that
for what you will.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:16.269
Whether it was intentional or not MegaUpload
would become one of the largest piracy sites

00:10:16.269 --> 00:10:19.980
in the world only beaten out by the likes
of the Pirate Bay.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:23.660
No one knew that it was actually Kim Dotcom
behind this company though.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:30.240
You see, Kim had registered the business under
an alias called Kim Tim Jim Vestor in Finland,

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.839
so as far as the public was concerned, it
run by some random Finnish dude.

00:10:34.839 --> 00:10:40.079
But, while Kim wasn’t getting any of the
credit or notoriety for creating MegaUpload,

00:10:40.079 --> 00:10:42.589
he was definitely getting the cash.

00:10:42.589 --> 00:10:46.610
The company was pulling in hundreds of millions
of dollars, most of which ended up with Kim

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:49.279
as he owned 68% of the business.

00:10:49.279 --> 00:10:53.730
He finally had the money that he always claimed
he had and he would use this fortune to buy

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.200
his way into New Zealand.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:11:00.430
You see, by purchasing $10 million worth of
New Zealand government bonds, he would get

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:04.150
himself placed into the high investment category
of immigration.

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:08.459
And once he was in, he would purchase a $24
million mansion just outside Auckland.

00:11:08.459 --> 00:11:13.730
But, the truth was that neither New Zealand
nor his neighbors were happy to have him.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:18.380
And Kim’s efforts to joke about his past
with his neighbors just made him look worse.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:22.660
In fact, he sent a letters to his neighbors
with the following “First of all let me

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:26.470
assure you that having a criminal Neighbor
like me comes with benefits.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:30.720
Our newly opened local money laundering facility
can help you with your tax fraud optimization.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.209
Our network of international insiders can
provide you with valuable stock tips."

00:11:35.209 --> 00:11:39.840
Let’s just say his neighbors didn’t find
this humor to be very funny.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:44.480
But, while New Zealand wasn’t a fan of Kim,
the internet very much was.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:49.410
And when it was revealed that he was the one
behind MegaUpload in 2011, he cemented himself

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.170
as an internet legend.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:56.269
He would go onto expand the Mega empire by
launching Megavideo, MegaPix, Megalive, Megapay

00:11:56.269 --> 00:11:57.959
and so on and so forth.

00:11:57.959 --> 00:12:03.960
But as far as the FBI was concerned, all of
this was just a Megafraud.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:10.120
On January 5, 2012, indictments would be filed
against Kim for racketeering, copyright infringement,

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.500
and money laundering.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:15.600
And two weeks later, New Zealand’s anti
terrorist squad would descend upon Kim’s

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:22.720
mega mansion and shutdown MegaUpload.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:30.300
MEGA.NZ
After the raid, Kim would be thrown into prison

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:31.300
at Mt.

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.950
Eden where he spent a month before being released
on bail.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.290
He didn’t have much to return to though.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:40.990
His wife would divorce him shortly after and
MegaUpload was completely shutdown.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:46.649
Not to mention, much of his property other
than his mansion had been seized by the police.

00:12:46.649 --> 00:12:51.370
But, despite the bleak situation, Kim would
fight back.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.889
His first goal was to take down the New Zealand
authorities because without their help, the

00:12:55.889 --> 00:12:58.480
FBI couldn’t really do anything.

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:02.730
Fortunately for Kim, this wasn’t too hard
as the authorities had broken a lot of protocol

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:05.529
due to pressure from the FBI.

00:13:05.529 --> 00:13:08.360
For one, they had been illegally spying on
him for weeks.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:12.899
Two, they literally came in with an anti terrorist
squad.

00:13:12.899 --> 00:13:16.029
Three, they unnecessarily seized his property.

00:13:16.029 --> 00:13:20.240
And four, they turned over this illegally
seized data over to the FBI.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:26.350
Kim’s lawyers would retaliate through all
four of these bases and more or less humiliate

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.620
the authorities for this raid.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:33.149
After about 5 years of this, New Zealand would
back off and simply agree to settle with Kim

00:13:33.149 --> 00:13:34.550
for an undisclosed amount.

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:39.560
The FBI, on the other hand, was not looking
to settle by any means.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:43.139
They were looking to extradite Kim to the
US and charge him with every copyright law

00:13:43.139 --> 00:13:44.470
they could think of.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:49.899
But, this requires going through a pretty
lengthy and often deadend extradition process

00:13:49.899 --> 00:13:53.449
which the FBI is still dealing with to this
day.

00:13:53.449 --> 00:13:55.029
Will he ever be extradited?

00:13:55.029 --> 00:13:57.620
Well, only time will tell.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:01.500
In the meantime though, Kim went ahead and
launched yet another file sharing platform

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:05.110
called Mega.nz with a couple of cofounders.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:10.019
And to really rub it into the face of authorities,
Kim would launch the site exactly one year

00:14:10.019 --> 00:14:12.490
after MegaUpload was shut down.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:17.480
And to be honest, Mega.nz is a pirate’s
dream.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:22.529
Unlike torrents which uses a peer to peer
network, Mega uses a server client network

00:14:22.529 --> 00:14:25.820
which makes it substantially harder to identify
pirates.

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:31.459
Also, everything is end to end encrypted which
again just makes it even harder.

00:14:31.459 --> 00:14:34.800
Little to say, Mega was a massive success.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:39.080
Within the first hour of launch, they would
attract a 100,000 users.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:43.329
Within a few days, this would grow to a million
users, and within a few years, this would

00:14:43.329 --> 00:14:45.670
grow to 35 million users.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:51.519
Today, Mega has over 200 million users and
stores 107 billion files.

00:14:51.519 --> 00:14:58.259
Now, with all that being said, I want to note
that Kim is no longer involved in Mega and

00:14:58.259 --> 00:15:02.639
Mega is very much trying to move away from
this association with piracy.

00:15:02.639 --> 00:15:06.930
They’re more than happy to takedown copyrighted
material from their platform as they truly

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:11.850
want to be seen as competitor to Dropbox,
Google Drive, iCloud, and OneDrive.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:16.190
But while I wish them the best of luck in
this transition, the reality is that a lot

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:18.430
of pirates still use Mega.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:23.440
In fact, there used to be a full on subreddit
called megalinks with over 30,000 links.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.160
And after reddit took down the subreddit,
the community just moved onto other social

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:30.810
media platforms and even their own dedicated
websites.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:36.269
So, Mega definitely still has quite a bit
of work to do and hopefully they’re able

00:15:36.269 --> 00:15:37.269
to.

00:15:37.269 --> 00:15:44.029
But in the meantime, Kim’s initial presence
is still very much weighing down the brand.

00:15:44.029 --> 00:15:53.240
KIM’S LEGACY:
Since leaving Mega, Kim has experimented with

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:56.810
some outlandish things like experimenting
with politics.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:16:01.890
He created a political party called Internet
Party but this didn’t really go anywhere.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:06.690
In fact, the party only won 499 votes in total
in 2017 election.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:11.389
There was also rumors that he was gonna launch
his own cryptocurrency but that never came

00:16:11.389 --> 00:16:12.699
to fruition either.

00:16:12.699 --> 00:16:17.010
